<SubSubSection title="Force-Deformation Relation" id="force-deformation_relation"> 

<DisplayEquation equation='\\delta = \\frac{PL}{EA}\\' title="Relation." background="True" derivation="True" id="axl-fdr">
    
    <DisplayEquation equation='P = \\sigma A\\' />
    <DisplayEquation equation='P = E \\varepsilon A\\' />
    <DisplayEquation equation='P = E\\frac{\\delta}{L}A\\' />

</DisplayEquation>

<DisplayEquation equation='\\delta = fP   =>   f = \\frac{L}{EA}\\' title=" Axial flexibility." background="True" />

<DisplayEquation equation='P = k\\delta   =>   k = \\frac{EA}{L}\\' title=" Axial stiffness." background="True" />

<strong> Axially Varying Properties </strong>
For non-uniform load, material property and cross-section area:

 <DisplayEquation equation='\\delta = \\int_0^L\\frac{F(x)}{E(x)A(x)}dx\\' title="Variable properties." id="sts-vpr" background="True" derivation="True" >

	 <DisplayEquation equation='\\sigma = E\\varepsilon\\' /> 
	 <DisplayEquation equation='\\frac{F(x)}{A(x)} = E(x)\\varepsilon(x)\\' /> 
	 <DisplayEquation equation='\\frac{F(x)}{A(x)} = E(x)\\frac{d\\delta(x)}{dx}\\' /> 
	 <DisplayEquation equation='d\\delta = \\frac{F(x)}{E(x)A(x)}dx\\' />

</DisplayEquation>

 Assume variations with <InlineEquation equation='x' /> are "mild" (on length scale longer than cross-sectional length scales)

